Chet is a font remapper for the MS-Dos compatible computer with
EGA or VGA screens. It allows you to create fonts in the 8x14 and 9x14
character set and doesn't take any memory.

Back in December I retrieved it from rec.games.rogue and, using
the rogue.814 font, create a nethack font (actually, three of them).

It changes the characters we use (like the double ~ for fountains) 
into a picture that, at least, looks more like a fountain. 

I created characters for most of the characters you see in the game
with the exception of the multiple use characters ( like '(' for all
types of weapons and '[' for all types of armor for example). Most
of the other characters are single use like the fountain and doorways.

I have received about 30 requests from people asking that I mail it.
I have been mailing it and then I sent it off to comp.binaries.ibm.pc
to be posted. The moderator (Bill) says that it usually takes about 
4-5 weeks for a post to go out. It still hasn't gone out. I just decided to
post it rather than wait and since we are the only group that seems
interested in it, I posted it here.

If you don't use MS-Dos computers, then I apologize for taking up 
your time.

